      "content": "it's just that the effort to stay \"on\" feels so violent now. like i'm constantly fighting against the natural way things should go. if the darkness is supposed to be this kind of freedom, why do people fight it so hard? why is it so much harder to just accept that the house is empty and let the last light go out?",
